import os, sys
LOOK = ("Look: real film still from a big-budget modern fantasy film, shot on 65mm film, real materials and textures, photoreal, a little bit nostalgic. "
        "Any visible text must be real words exactly as printed in a dictionary or a published newspaper.")
P = [
# 1 balloon harbor above the clouds
"Cinematic photorealistic fantasy, where lost things go: every balloon a child ever let slip from their hand ends up here. High above a sea of soft golden sunset clouds floats an old wooden harbor pier, and tied along its long railings by their strings are tens of thousands of real helium balloons of every color, gently bobbing in the wind like a vast field of floating flowers, red, yellow, sky blue, pink, silver. An old balloon keeper with a white beard, wearing a weathered navy coat and a flat cap, walks slowly along the pier carefully tying one newly arrived red balloon to the railing, with the gentle face of someone keeping something precious safe until it can be returned. Far below, through a gap in the clouds, tiny city lights are visible. Camera: eye-level medium-wide shot along the pier, 35mm lens, deep focus, the keeper in the lower right third, the endless rows of balloons stretching into the sunset. Lighting: warm low golden sunset light glowing through the colorful balloons, soft rim light on the old man, pink and gold clouds. Color palette: golden sunset, rainbow balloons, weathered wood brown, navy coat, fine film grain. " + LOOK,
# 2 island of lost teddy bears
"Cinematic photorealistic fantasy, where lost things go: every teddy bear and stuffed toy a child ever lost ends up on this quiet island. A long, calm beach at golden sunset, and sitting in neat patient rows on the soft sand, all facing the sea, are hundreds of real worn plush toys: old teddy bears with patched elbows and one button eye, floppy rabbits, knitted elephants, a faded giraffe, each well loved and slightly worn, as if waiting for a boat to bring their children back. In the foreground, one small old brown teddy bear sits a little apart, a tiny boat of folded newspaper at its feet, the gentle waves almost touching it. Camera: low eye-level shot from the sand just behind the front row of toys, 35mm lens, deep focus, the small teddy bear sharp in the foreground left, the long rows of toys and the glowing sea beyond. Lighting: warm low golden sunset light from the sea, soft rim light on the fuzzy plush, long gentle shadows on the sand. Color palette: golden sunset, soft pastel plush colors, warm sand beige, calm blue-silver sea, fine film grain. " + LOOK,
# 3 valley of balls kicked over the fence
"Cinematic photorealistic fantasy, where lost things go: every ball that ever flew over a fence, onto a roof or into the neighbor's yard ends up in this quiet green valley. Rolling hills covered with millions of real balls, scuffed soccer balls, faded tennis balls, baseballs with grass stains, beach balls, basketballs, a red rubber playground ball, gathered in drifts like colorful pebbles on a riverbank. An old groundskeeper in overalls and a straw hat sits on a wooden crate in the middle of the valley, carefully polishing a worn baseball with a cloth and looking at it with a warm, nostalgic smile, a wicker basket of sorted tennis balls beside him. Camera: eye-level medium-wide shot, 35mm lens, deep focus, the old man in the lower center, the endless hills of balls rolling away to the horizon under a big summer sky. Lighting: soft warm late-afternoon summer light, long gentle shadows across the hills of balls, a few puffy white clouds. Color palette: grass green, faded leather brown, tennis ball yellow, sky blue, warm straw, fine film grain. " + LOOK,
# 4 snowy forest of single mittens
"Cinematic photorealistic fantasy, where lost things go: every single glove and mitten that ever lost its partner ends up in this snowy forest. A quiet birch forest in deep winter, soft snow falling, and hanging from every branch like colorful leaves are thousands of real single mittens and gloves: red knitted mittens, striped wool gloves, tiny baby mittens on strings, leather work gloves, a pink ski glove. In a small clearing, a kind old woman in a thick knitted shawl stands beside a wooden cart, holding up two mismatched red mittens side by side and comparing them closely, gently trying to find each lonely mitten its pair, a few already-matched pairs tied together with yarn in her cart. Camera: eye-level medium-wide shot, 50mm lens, deep focus, the old woman in the right third, the mitten-covered trees filling the soft white forest. Lighting: soft diffused winter daylight, a warm glow from a small lantern on her cart, snowflakes catching the light. Color palette: snow white, birch silver, warm red and rainbow wool, cream shawl, lantern amber, fine film grain. " + LOOK,
# 5 underwater lost and found
"Cinematic photorealistic fantasy comedy, where lost things go: everything people ever dropped off a boat or lost at the beach ends up at the lost-and-found counter at the bottom of the sea. On the sandy sea floor in clear turquoise water sits a small old wooden lost-and-found desk with a brass service bell, and behind it a real giant octopus works as the clerk, calmly sorting with all eight arms at once: one arm holds up a pair of sunglasses, another a single flip-flop, another a wedding ring, another a smartphone, another a set of car keys, another a child's plastic shovel. Behind the desk, tall shelves made of coral and old crates hold hundreds of lost sunglasses, hats, watches and phones, and a small queue of curious fish waits in front of the counter. Camera: eye-level medium shot on the sea floor, 35mm lens, deep focus, the octopus and the desk in the center, the shelves behind. Lighting: soft sunlight filtering down through the clear water, dancing caustic light patterns on the sand and the desk, gentle blue depth. Color palette: turquoise water, sand beige, octopus coral red, brass gold, colorful lost objects, fine film grain. " + LOOK,
]
m = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 'text2image_soul_v2'
d = 'v1'
os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
open(f'{d}/prompts.txt', 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='\n').write('\n'.join(P) + '\n')
open(f'{d}/model.txt', 'w').write(m + '\n')
open(f'{d}/aspect.txt', 'w').write('3:2\n')
print(m, [len(p.split()) for p in P])
